clocksource: bcm2835: report a deadline that passed while programming it

The system timer compare only matches on equality. If more than the
minimum delta elapses between reading the counter and writing the
compare, the event fires only after the 32-bit counter wraps, about
71 minutes later, and every timer on the system stalls with it. Under
QEMU a vCPU stall during host I/O is enough. Return -ETIME so the
clockevents core reprograms with a larger delta.

--- a/drivers/clocksource/bcm2835_timer.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/bcm2835_timer.c
@@ -45,9 +45,15 @@
 {
 	struct bcm2835_timer *timer = container_of(evt_dev,
 		struct bcm2835_timer, evt);
-	writel_relaxed(readl_relaxed(system_clock) + event,
-		timer->compare);
-	return 0;
+	u32 next = readl_relaxed(system_clock) + event;
+
+	writel_relaxed(next, timer->compare);
+	/*
+	 * The compare only fires on an exact match: a deadline that passed
+	 * while it was written would wait for the 32-bit counter to wrap.
+	 */
+	return event < 0x7fffffff &&
+		(s32)(next - readl_relaxed(system_clock)) <= 0 ? -ETIME : 0;
 }
 
 static irqreturn_t bcm2835_time_interrupt(int irq, void *dev_id)
